    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Talking about travel plans",
     "texto": [
      "Skal + infinitive expresses a plan: Jeg skal reise («I am going to travel»). After skal, the verb is in the infinitive without å, unlike English «going to travel».",
      "Fly means «plane» and flyplass means «airport». Pass means «passport», not «pass»: it looks like the English word «pass», but the meaning is different."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
